Follow `docs/for-agents/HARD-RULES.md`, `AGENTS.md` (pickup contract, lanes, Agent packet) and `AGENTS-MCS.md`. In short: pulled data never goes in git (local `local-data/` only); owner fields are names only, never values (D-13); public publish or deploy needs Morgen's per-jurisdiction beta-gate sign-off (NA-269) while publish/deploy tooling may be built and tested (HARD-RULES 3); MPAC- and NPCA-derived data may be pulled and used, all fields pulled and identifying information screened at publish (HARD-RULES 2, 4, 5); no workaround for gated sources; agents never merge. Open questions are in `heavymap-planning/OPEN-DECISIONS.md`: don't decide them.

For concurrent frontend/Atlas tasks, also follow `heavymap-planning/WORKING-AGREEMENT.md` (scoped UI authorization, direct-assignment packets, contract-change ownership and track-specific insights). PR #80 records the merged split plan; split execution and identifier migration require a separate assignment from Morgen.

Process insights (standing rule): Before finishing a session or PR, record reusable findings once with live-verified evidence. Atlas findings go to `Spreadsheets/19-process-insights.csv` with `PI-` IDs. Frontend findings use `heavymap-planning/frontend/19-process-insights.csv` with `HM-PI-` IDs; until that file exists, use the PR's Process insights section with the same columns. Never write frontend findings into Atlas sheet 19. Preserve reserved IDs and append-only etiquette. If unable to write, report findings in the final response for transfer. See `heavymap-planning/PROCESS-INSIGHTS.md`.
